# ============================================================================
# TinySMS: on an Android phone, the email-to-text gateway; on a computer or in
# a browser, the console that sends texts through it.
#
# ON THE PHONE (the gateway)
#
#   Email your tinymail address with "sms: 07700 900123" in the subject and
#   the message in the body: this phone texts it. When they text back, the
#   reply is emailed to whoever sent the message, and replying to that email
#   texts them again.
#
#   Sign in once with your tiny-web account. From then on the server pushes
#   this phone the moment a text is waiting (Firebase), and the phone asks
#   every few seconds as well in case a push goes astray.
#   Texts that arrive are passed to the server as they come. It keeps going
#   with the screen off, with a notice in the phone's list saying so.
#
#   What it uses, all through Vml(...):
#     Fetch            the TinySMS server (tiny-web.uk), as JSON
#     SmsSend, OnSms   texts out and in: an app exported for Android only
#     LookupNames      names for the numbers on a screen (the console, the web page) or a reply's sender,
#                      from the phone's own address book
#     ReadContacts,    the names in the address book (names only: numbers stay on the phone) go to the
#     LookupNumber     account so the console and web page can text people by name; the phone finds the
#                      number itself when it sends
#     OnMessages       replies that came by chat (RCS), read from the messaging app's notices
#     OnPush           woken by the server when a text is waiting (no text goes through Google: the
#                      push only says "ask now")
#     RunInBackground  keep going while the phone is in a pocket
#
# ON A COMPUTER OR IN A BROWSER (the console)
#   Sign in with the same tiny-web account: write texts at a keyboard, see each
#   conversation as it happens, and see whether the gateway phone is awake.
#   The texts still go out from the phone: this copy never sends or receives
#   one itself, and never signs in as a gateway.
#
#   Made with Visualised. The scripts are at the bottom; "Start" runs first.
# ============================================================================

@Window TinySMS
Title=TinySMS
Version=2.7
Width=360
Height=640
OnOpened=Start
AndroidPackage=io.visualised.made.tinysms.k7b1ce6cd
AndroidKey=7b1ce6cd

@MenuTheme theme
Parent=TinySMS
Background=#0F766E

@Canvas c
Parent=TinySMS
Width=360
Height=640
Background=#FFFFFF

@TextBlock lblTitle
Parent=c
Canvas.Left=12
Canvas.Top=8
Width=336
Height=30
FontSize=22
FontWeight=Bold
Text=TinySMS

@TextBlock lblState
Parent=c
Canvas.Left=12
Canvas.Top=42
Width=336
Height=56
FontSize=17
TextWrapping=Wrap
Text=

# --- signing in: once, with the tiny-web account -----------------------------

@TextBox txtUser
